{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/attachingyourownfiles"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenClipKit"}],"title":"Attaching your own files"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Attaching-your-own-data","title":"Attaching your own data","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext"],"generated":true}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add your app’s own state to every report, so the agent sees what the screenshot can’t show."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Your app knows things ScreenClip can’t see: the signed-in account, what’s in the cart, which feature flags are on, the last request the backend answered. Register an attachment provider and its files travel with every report, next to the built-in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#if DEBUG","ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"cart\") { context in","  let cart = await MainActor.run { CartStore.shared.snapshot }  \/\/ any Encodable","  return [try .json(cart, name: \"cart\", summary: \"the cart's \\(cart.items.count) items and promo codes\")]","}","#endif"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The agent reads each file’s name and summary in its prompt. It opens a file only when the screenshot and note aren’t enough, so write the summary for it: say what is inside.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Attachment providers need ScreenClipKit 1.2.0 or later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"When-the-provider-runs","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"When the provider runs"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach logs and diagnostics"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" enabled, the provider starts when the report sheet opens. It can read the app state while the tester annotates. Turning diagnostics on later starts a fresh provider run with the same report ID and capture time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"After ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", ScreenClip waits up to ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" more (5 seconds by default, at most 30) with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Saving report…"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" on screen. It then sends the report without whatever hasn’t arrived.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The provider runs off the main actor. Read main-actor state with ","type":"text"},{"code":"await MainActor.run { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and keep heavy work out of that closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Several-files-async-work-and-context","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Several files, async work, and context"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A provider returns any number of attachments. Return an empty array to add nothing this time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"account\", timeout: .seconds(10)) { context in","  let session = await MainActor.run { Session.current }","  guard let session else { return [] }","  let flags = try await FeatureFlags.shared.current()","  APILog.shared.mark(\"ScreenClip report \\(context.reportID)\")","  return [","    try .json(session.debugSummary, name: \"account\", summary: \"signed-in account, plan, and region\"),","    .text(flags.description, name: \"feature-flags\", summary: \"remote feature flags in effect\"),","    .text(await APILog.shared.recent(20), name: \"api-requests\", summary: \"last 20 backend requests and status codes\"),","  ]","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" carries the report’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"reportID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"capturedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"screenTitle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"screenPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Log the report id next to your own records, such as a backend request id or an analytics session, to tie them to the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Cancellation-and-failure","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Cancellation and failure"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The provider is cancelled when the tester cancels the report, or turns off ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach logs and diagnostics"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". Use cancellable APIs or check ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task.isCancelled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the provider throws or misses its timeout, only its own files are left out. The report is still sent, and a line is logged under the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenClipKit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" subsystem.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registering-and-removing","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Registering and removing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each id holds one provider. Registering the same id again replaces it, so calling ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" from an initializer or ","type":"text"},{"code":"onAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is safe. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" removes it. Providers run concurrently, and their files are listed in registration order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Names-and-limits","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Names and limits"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" becomes a file name the Mac accepts. It is lowercased, anything other than letters, digits, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" becomes ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and it is cut to 32 characters, plus ","type":"text"},{"code":".txt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":".json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A name already in use, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"logs.txt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or another provider’s, gets ","type":"text"},{"code":"-2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"-3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and so on.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each attachment can be up to 1 MB (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Larger ones are left out.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A report takes up to 16 attachments (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumCount","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Later ones are left out.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All files in a report share a 4 MB limit. When a report is over it, the largest files are dropped first.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"What-not-to-attach","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What not to attach"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t attach secrets. On the Mac, token-like strings are hidden in text files, but JSON files are stored as sent. Any attached file can be read by an agent working on the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Release builds ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" does nothing, and the closure is never called. Keep the call inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" anyway, so the code that gathers the data stays out of Release too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/AttachingYourOwnFiles"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipReportContext":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipreportcontext","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","title":"ScreenClipReportContext","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenClipReportContext","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenClipReportContext","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"What a provider knows about the report it is attaching to.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/removeattachmentprovider(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stops adding the files from the provider registered with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"removeAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Report what you see in your own iOS app, straight into ScreenClip on your Mac, where a coding agent fixes it."}],"images":[{"identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg","type":"icon"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit","title":"ScreenClipKit","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachmentprovider","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collects your app’s own attachments for a report. It runs off the main actor; read main-actor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state with "},{"code":"await MainActor.run { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Throwing leaves this provider’s files out of the report."}],"title":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"}]},"screenclip-icon.svg":{"identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/screenclip-icon.svg","traits":["1x","light"]}],"alt":"The ScreenClip icon","type":"image"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/Diagnostics":{"abstract":[{"text":"The optional files ScreenClipKit attaches, and how the tester controls them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","title":"Diagnostics","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/diagnostics","role":"article"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumBytes":{"role":"symbol","title":"maximumBytes","abstract":[{"text":"The largest attachment ScreenClip sends. Larger ones are left out of the report.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumbytes","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumBytes"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumCount":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumcount","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumCount","title":"maximumCount","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The most attachments ScreenClip sends with one report, across all providers. Later ones are left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","title":"ScreenClipAttachment","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenClipAttachment","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A file your app adds to a report, next to ScreenClip’s own logs and diagnostics."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/setattachmentprovider(_:timeout:_:)","title":"setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Adds your app’s own files to every report: state, records, anything an agent would want","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to see next to the screenshot.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"timeout","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","preciseIdentifier":"s:13ScreenClipKit0aB18AttachmentProvidera","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"}}}